# Google "Continue with Google" — Web OAuth client ID
#
# Wisp lets users back up their nsec to a hidden folder in their own
# Google Drive (encrypted with a 4–8 digit PIN). To enable that flow
# you need two OAuth clients from Google Cloud Console:
#
#   1. Web application client — its client ID goes in THIS file.
#   2. iOS application client — its client ID goes in
#      google-ios-client-id.txt (see google-ios-client-id.txt.example).
#
# The Web client ID is set as `serverClientID` on GIDConfiguration so the
# ID token's audience matches what the Android app sees. Without this,
# the `sub` claim a user gets on iOS would differ from Android and
# cross-platform backup restore would fail.
#
# To use this file:
#   - Visit https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials and create
#     (or reuse) a Web application OAuth 2.0 client. Use the same client
#     that the Android Wisp app uses so backups round-trip across
#     platforms — copy it from
#     ~/dev/wisp/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml (look for
#     `google_web_client_id`).
#   - Save your client ID (looks like
#     1234567890-abc...xyz.apps.googleusercontent.com) to
#     wisp/Resources/google-web-client-id.txt (no quotes, single line).
#   - Also enable the Google Drive API for your project so the
#     drive.appdata scope works.
#
# This file (the .example) is checked in. The real file
# (google-web-client-id.txt) is gitignored.
